{
  "id": 322373795,
  "iid": 16919,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "PDU Transport: Use curr_proto_layer_num instead of curr_layer_num",
  "description": "When a Signal PDU has no payload configured, the dissector calls `call_data_dissector` and that increments `curr_layer_num`.\n\nThe PDU Transport dissector used `curr_layer_num` to check if other PDUs were already added at that depth and add a comma to separate them in the info column, but this failed if the Signal PDU dissector found that the payload was not configured for that PDU.\n\nSwitching to `curr_proto_layer_num` fixes the issue.\n\nI'm not sure if this is the correct approach. Any suggestion is accepted.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2024-08-21T08:11:22.707Z",
  "updated_at": "2024-08-24T08:49:43.464Z",
