    {
      "id": "5d61939ec8b7451d891c789919b64063793f38eb",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2073301631,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The dissector checks if it's the first time running (at this depth), and if not appends a comma and a space before writing to the info column, so the output looks like this:\n> PDU (ID: 0x1, NAME1), PDU (ID: 0x2, NAME2), PDU (ID: 0x3, NAME3)\n\ninstead of:\n> PDU (ID: 0x1, NAME1)PDU (ID: 0x2, NAME2)PDU (ID: 0x3, NAME3)\n\nHowever, if in this example PDU 0x2 has no payload configured, the dissector calls `call_data_dissector` and that increments `curr_layer_num`. Now, when decoding PDU 0x3, the dissector thinks it's at another layer and the output will look like this:\n> PDU (ID: 0x1, NAME1), PDU (ID: 0x2, NAME2)PDU (ID: 0x3, NAME3)\n\nSwitching to `curr_proto_layer_num` fixes the issue because it doesn't increment externally.",
          "author": {
            "id": 18219493,
            "username": "giovanni.musto",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Giovanni Musto",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b8ca1135be5e614246a54ed49c6809a9b172aafdcb27c2db7ec5548b625e76d5?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/giovanni.musto"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-08-23T13:18:57.829Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-08-24T08:49:18.896Z",
